   I want to complain about something that while not exactly a bug, is a rather
undesirable (in my opinion) feature of nethack.  I find it particularly
noticeable in version 3.0 (does food take londer to eat??) but is present
in previous versions.  That is that eating is "uninterruptable"; i.e. when
a monster shows up, you keep on eating, no matter how badly it's pounding
you.  This is in contrast to what happens when you are, say digging with
a pick axe, opening a tin, etc. where you stop whatever you are doing when
a monster appears next to you.  It doesn't seem like it should be too hard
to add "improved" eating, maybe as a compiler option.  What about it??

  -- Alex Ridgway


